# IIQ Project Scope

This rule complements the generic `agent-flow.mdc` with IIQ-specific project
constraints. When this pack is installed, every agent run loads both the
generic pipeline rules and these IIQ-specific scope rules.

## Project context

All agents run in the identityiq repo only.

**Tech stack:**
- Frontend: AngularJS (legacy), Angular 18 (modern), ExtJS (admin pages)
- Backend: Java + Spring + Hibernate
- Build: JSPM (AngularJS), Angular CLI (Angular 18), Ant (Java + full UI)

**Primary paths:**
- `web/ui/js/` — frontend source
- `src/sailpoint/` — Java backend source
- `tools/` — Angular 18 build tooling

## Build safety

**NEVER run destructive targets:**

- `ant deploy*` — any deploy target
- `ant -f DevRebuild.xml` and any of its targets — **drops and recreates databases**

## Allowed build commands

- **Surgeon (Java / AngularJS / XHTML):** `ant core` + `ant build`
  Java compile + full UI/JS build, per-task verification.
- **Surgeon (Angular 18 fast iteration):** `cd tools && npx gulp dev-build`
  UI only, no Java — fastest feedback loop for Angular 18 work.
- **Surgeon (Angular 18 full):** `ant ui-build -Dui.development=true`
  Full UI build via Ant.
- **Surgeon (Angular 18 quality):** `cd tools && npx gulp ui-quality`
  ESLint + Prettier.
- **Review:** `ant clean build`
  Clean slate, final gate — catches stale artifacts.
- **Tests:** `ant jstests` (legacy JS unit tests),
  `cd tools && npx gulp tests` (Angular 18 tests — note: no `.spec.ts` files exist yet).

## Ticket prefix

Ticket prefixes are extracted directly from the trigger at runtime — no
whitelist config. `@orchestrator.md Work on IIQMAG-1234` → prefix `IIQMAG`.

Branch prefix + base-branch conventions are per-team config in
`contexts/config/pipeline.iiq.yaml → runtime.branching`:

- `runtime.branching.prefix_story` — e.g. `"feature/"`
- `runtime.branching.prefix_bug` — e.g. `"fix/"`
- `runtime.branching.base_branch` — e.g. `"develop"` or `"main"`

Orchestrator composes branch names as `{prefix_story}{PREFIX}-{NUM}-{slug}`
(or `{prefix_bug}...` for bugs). Do NOT hardcode a specific ticket prefix in
prose or examples — extract it from the live trigger.

## Additional scope rules

Team boundaries, active migrations, reference implementations, and coding
norms not captured in layer-specific standards skills live in
`contexts/project-context.md`, not this file. This file is the
stable project scope; `project-context.md` is the living project knowledge.
